// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row rc_coerce_unsized_source_not_moved (tier 2). AN
// UNSIZE COERCION OF A USER SMART POINTER — `Rc<A>` -> `Rc<dyn Tr>` — DOES NOT
// CONSUME ITS SOURCE, SO THE SOURCE BINDING IS STILL USABLE AND IS DROPPED A
// SECOND TIME, READING AND WRITING THE REFCOUNT CELL AFTER IT WAS FREED.
//
// Measured 2026-09-08 on build 8e5f92705b285d29 43, reducing the CORRUPT
// verdict on tests/spec/pass/coerce_4 (9 invalid accesses, rc 0) from the
// valgrind sweep — unrowed_backlog entry `vg_corrupt_coerce_4`.
//
// THE RUNTIME HALF, three spellings, same binary, valgrind
// (sandbox/vg-round2/hand/): `take_rc_dyn(rc7)` — implicit coercion at a call
// argument — 3 invalid accesses; `let d: Rc<dyn Sp> = rc as Rc<dyn Sp>;` — an
// explicit `as` — 3; the same in an inner scope — 3. Each is an Invalid read
// of size 4, an Invalid write of size 4 and an Invalid read of size 4 inside
// `Rc$G1$A__drop_rc`, at a block already free'd by `Rc$G1$udyn_Sp__drop_rc`.
// There is NO double free: the second decrement takes the count 0 -> -1, so
// nothing aborts. rc is 0 and stdout is right — no gate in this tree sees it.
//
// CONTROLS, correct on the SAME binary:
//   * the same call WITHOUT a coercion — `fn take_rc_a(r: Rc<A>)` — 0 errors,
//     so the move is honoured when no unsizing happens.
//   * `Box<A> as Box<dyn Sp>` passed to a `Box<dyn Sp>` callee — 0 errors, so
//     the builtin Box unsize DOES consume its source. It is CoerceUnsized
//     through a user struct that does not.
//
// THE COMPILE-TIME HALF IS THIS PROGRAM, and it is the half a gate can read:
// after the coercion the source `rc` is USED AGAIN and the compile is silent.
// rustc: E0382, "borrow of moved value: `rc`" / "value used here after move".
// The two halves are one root — the coercion is not recorded as a move — and
// the `admits` spelling is chosen because the runtime spelling exits 0.
package rc_coerce_unsized_source_not_moved;
use logos.lang.rc;

trait Sp { fn v(&self) -> i64; }
struct A { x: i64 }
impl Sp for A { fn v(&self) -> i64 { return self.x; } }

fn main() -> i64 {
    let rc: Rc<A> = rc_new(A { x: 3i64 });
    let d: Rc<dyn Sp> = rc as Rc<dyn Sp>;
    if d.v() != 3i64 { return 1i64; }
    if rc.v() != 3i64 { return 2i64; }   // USE AFTER MOVE — rustc: E0382
    return 0i64;
}
